## 1. GraphQL Normalized Cache Memory Topology

```text
Incoming Query Response:
{
  "order": {
    "__typename": "Order", "id": "901", "total": 150.00,
    "customer": { "__typename": "User", "id": "42", "name": "Alice" }
  }
}

IN-MEMORY NORMALIZED GRAPH:
┌────────────────────────┐
│      NORMALIZED STORE  │
├────────────────────────┤
│ "Order:901" ───────────┼──▶ { id: "901", total: 150.00, customer: "User:42" }
│ "User:42"   ───────────┼──▶ { id: "42", name: "Alice" }
└────────────────────────┘
            ▲
            │ (Mutation updates User:42 name to "Alice Smith")
            │
[ Both OrderScreen and ProfileScreen instantly re-render with "Alice Smith"! ]
```
